      "hints": [
        "Differentiate $f(x) = (4x + 1)^{3/2}$ to get $f'(x) = 6(4x + 1)^{1/2}$.",
        "Differentiate again to get $f''(x) = 12(4x + 1)^{-1/2}$."
      ],
      "walkthrough": [
        "Differentiate $f(x) = (4x + 1)^{\\frac{3}{2}}$ with respect to $x$ using the chain rule:\n$$f'(x) = \\frac{3}{2}(4x + 1)^{\\frac{1}{2}} \\times (4) = 6(4x + 1)^{\\frac{1}{2}}$$",
        "Differentiate a second time to find $f''(x)$:\n$$f''(x) = 6\\left(\\frac{1}{2}\\right)(4x + 1)^{-\\frac{1}{2}} \\times (4) = 12(4x + 1)^{-\\frac{1}{2}} = \\frac{12}{\\sqrt{4x + 1}}$$"
      ],
      "checking": {
