        "Evaluate $T_1 = f(2) = 27$, $T_2 = f'(2) = 18$, and $T_3 = k f''(2) = 4k$.",
        "Equate common ratios: $\\frac{18}{27} = \\frac{4k}{18} \\implies k = 3$."
      ],
      "walkthrough": [
        "Evaluate each term at $x = 2$:\n$$T_1 = f(2) = (4(2) + 1)^{\\frac{3}{2}} = 9^{\\frac{3}{2}} = 27$$\n$$T_2 = f'(2) = 6(4(2) + 1)^{\\frac{1}{2}} = 6(9^{\\frac{1}{2}}) = 6(3) = 18$$\n$$T_3 = k f''(2) = k \\left(\\frac{12}{\\sqrt{4(2) + 1}}\\right) = k\\left(\\frac{12}{3}\\right) = 4k$$",
        "Set up the common ratio condition for a geometric progression:\n$$\\frac{T_2}{T_1} = \\frac{T_3}{T_2} \\implies \\frac{18}{27} = \\frac{4k}{18}$$\n$$\\frac{2}{3} = \\frac{4k}{18} \\implies 4k = 18 \\times \\frac{2}{3} = 12 \\implies k = 3$$"
